Google services the demo calls
  Gemini on Vertex AI (grammar compiler, voice shelf check, district officer's brief),
  Cloud Run, BigQuery, Google Maps Routes API, Pub/Sub (the live feed, once deploy/live.sh is run).

Real data
  anumaan/realcheck_england.json holds monthly totals per integrated care board drawn from the
  English Prescribing Dataset, NHS Business Services Authority Open Data Portal
  (https://opendata.nhsbsa.net/dataset/english-prescribing-data-epd), fetched 30 September 2026.
  Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0.
  The file lists the official shortage notices it relies on, each with its source.

Reports the Kerala replay follows (anumaan/scenario.py; the replay's records are synthetic)
  Onmanorama, 22 September 2026, "Bureaucratic paralysis chokes medicine supplies in
  government hospitals"; Onmanorama, 29 September 2026, "Medicine stocks available at
  hospitals, shortage at KMSCL warehouses: DMOs inform health minister". Quoted briefly, with links.

Source documents for the compiled grammar (grammar/crg/compiled.json)
  The PDFs are not redistributed here; grammar/sources/urls.txt lists where each came from.
  Each rule in compiled.json cites its source file, page and a short quote.
  - Indian Council of Medical Research: Standard Treatment Workflows for acute respiratory
    infection in adults, hypertension in adults, and urinary tract infections.
  - Ministry of Health and Family Welfare: Anemia Mukt Bharat operational guidelines (2018).
  - NCDC / MoHFW: NPCDCS training module for medical officers (2017), via NHSRC.
  - National Health Systems Resource Centre: training module for community health officers
    on acute simple illnesses (2022).
  grammar/crg/tracer.json is hand-written; the compiler only uses its condition and drug names.
